WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.235
To understand the importance of events

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.536
in Russia this weekend.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.005
We have to turn the clock back

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.439
a bit to 2014.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.607
When the Wagner group

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.908
was first identified

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.811
fighting to seize Crimea from Ukraine.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:12.812
At the time

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.914
it was thought to have about 5000 troops

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.883
fighting mostly in Africa

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.118
and the Middle East.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.519
Fast forward now to January

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.121
when the Ukraine and Ukraine,

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.689
the UK Ministry of Defense

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.823
put its numbers

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.960
at 50,000 fighters in Ukraine alone.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.963
Those troops, most were recruited from

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.830
Russian prisons

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.999
played a crucial role in the war,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.200
particularly in places

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.402
like Parma in the east,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.903
where some of the bloodiest and longest

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.239
battles of the war took place.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:39.839
With me here

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:40.807
now is former

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.375
US Director of National Intelligence

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.877
James Clapper.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.812
Years of experience, decades,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.547
I should say, looking into Russia

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.314
and what's happening there.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.550
Thanks so much for joining us. Jim.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.920
So first on Putin's leadership, is Putin

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.089
does he emerge from here

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.291
irreparably damaged?

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.660
Well, he's clearly damaged I think

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.296
irreparably remains to be seen.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.230
I think we're

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.432
perhaps rushing

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.299
to judgment here

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.601
about the end of Vladimir Putin.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.470
And I don't

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.005
I think it's a little early to do that.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:15.442
But clearly, his stature, his prestige,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.444
his image is diminished

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.946
both internationally and in domestically,

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.315
which is

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.283
one of the reasons

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.217
why I don't think he's going

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.387
to let Ghosn run around free and easy.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.590
What is the fate of the Wagner Group,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.526
which has enormous military influence

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.128
and its role in Ukraine

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.463
central, its role in Syria,

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.597
the war in Syria, central,

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.498
its role in several

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.366
little wars in Africa

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.335
that Russia has interests in Central.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.203
But also Prigozhin,

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.537
with his own power center

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.907
in Saudi inside Russia are Prigozhin

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.975
and the Wagner Group

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.811
now themselves irreparably damaged?

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.680
Well, that remains to be seen.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.082
And as a group, a critical question is

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.252
what is the fate of the Wagner group?

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.989
And as you indicated, in Ukraine,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.824
they're the most effective fighting force

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.426
that the Russians have had.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.627
And they're very active.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.262
And from the Russian standpoint,

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.464
very effective and lots of other areas

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.166
that you enumerated.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.501
So that's a great question.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.102
What is going to happen to them?

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.738
They are ostensibly under the loose

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.241
egis of the GRU

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.009
Military Intelligence Organization,

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.078
which also controls the Spetsnaz,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.280
their special operations forces.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.381
So there is

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.750
somewhat of a functional kinship there.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.987
And whether the Russian government

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:34.554
would attempt

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.823
to have a more more control

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.291
over the volunteer group

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.660
and its activities by tethering it

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.128
to some element

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.097
of the government, ministry of defense

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.533
or whatever remains to be seen.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.736
But it's clearly

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.404
this is a big problem for the Russians

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.206
because of its effectiveness.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:53.840
No question.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:55.275
So the

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.645
public story is that Prigozhin peacefully

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.414
ended his advance towards Moscow,

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.050
has taken a deal to go to Belarus,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.984
and some of his forces

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.252
are going to sign up with regular

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.421
Russian army units

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.857
and promotion's going to live safely

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.192
in Belarus.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.893
Do you buy that deal?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.296
Well, Jim,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.697
maybe I spent too much time

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.332
in intelligence with this whole thing.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.068
This deal to me is kind of fishy

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.938
that all of a sudden goes and stopped.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.274
Turn left or turn back.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.109
And then he's going to go to agreed

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.312
to go all of all places, Belarus,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.213
which is essentially

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.614
from a security standpoint

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.783
or an extension of Russia.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.786
I just I just wonder whether

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.555
it was a deal or somehow

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.959
behind the scenes, Putin exerted some

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.562
some form of leverage over Burgos and

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.431
that caused him to fall.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.399
This is an

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.534
unanswered question,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.869
obviously, and hopefully, as as

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.071
we learn more, we'll find out

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:58.771
just what happened.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:02.041
But on its face, it's all fishy to me.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.410
For a moment this weekend,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.778
I know that Western intelligence

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.613
was looking at this.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.680
And speaking of open

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.749
military confrontation

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.285
in Russia, there are still militias.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.453
There's still a Wagner militia.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.788
There's still other militias,

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.690
other potential challengers

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.691
to Putin's leadership,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.158
or at least

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.494
it's the factional fighting there.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.362
Does the U.S., does

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.463
the West have to prepare for

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:23.696
at least

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.098
the possibility

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.100
of Russia becoming a failed state?

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:28.868
Well, absolutely.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.168
I mean,

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.470
and there are those out there,

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.739
the Russia watchers, who

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:33.773
already are saying

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.641
this could easily

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:35.808
be the beginning

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.877
of the end of the Russian Federation.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.379
I personally think that, again,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.648
it's a little premature, but it could be.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:43.716
And as far as the U.S.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.417
government

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.886
needs to be prepared for all those

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.055
all those options

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.090
above at all, though, from,

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:51.858
let's say this from

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.593
an intelligence standpoint,

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.728
anytime you have a nuclear power

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:56.863
in a situation

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.698
like this, you get real sense of

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:02.201
about the status of their nuclear forces.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.003
So that'll be

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:04.604
on board

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.839
your uppermost in the minds of you

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.874
intelligence community.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.376
Was there at any point,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.111
do you think this weekend

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:12.645
the threat

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.680
that Russia's

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.549
nuclear weapons were at risk?

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.785
No. No, I didn't.

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.153
I didn't.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.721
And I felt that way from

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.922
ever since the invasion

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.391
that while despite the threats

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.526
that obviously

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.593
the probability

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.762
of the use of nuclear weapons is

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.497
is not zero, but it's still pretty low.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.833
And I don't think this situation

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.602
changed that their U.S.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.737
intelligence folks

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.205
have told me for some time

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.341
that if Putin were to lose power,

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.210
he's far more likely to face a threat

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.578
from his right flank

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.680
than from any sort of progressive,

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.450
you know, inside the country.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.819
If he were to leave power

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.923
Who what kind of person is yourself from?

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.424
What category

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.493
would be most likely to replace him?

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:00.893
Would it be

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.795
someone more aggressive, more?

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:05.031
Well, I would

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.599
I think it would

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:08.868
it would all depend

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:12.405
on the circumstances of his departure.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.074
If he were to do the part of all.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:15.908
You know, he does

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.443
have a close inner circle,

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.512
which is held together pretty well.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:20.980
I've always wondered

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.482
about his national security

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.684
adviser or equivalent Petruchio

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.086
as whether he might emerge,

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.522
but a long time crony KGB

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.624
crony of Putin's

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.762
So but I agree,

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.463
I think with you that the

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.866
the of the two theories

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.136
on attack

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.972
of some sort from the right

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.974
is more likely then than the left.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:48.641
Final question,

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.343
if I can, in terms of the effect

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.378
on the ongoing war in Ukraine,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:55.415
if you were advising Ukrainian leaders

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:56.315
now, military

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.917
commanders, would you say

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.552
now's the time to strike even harder?

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.320
Well, actually, not.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.855
I think I'd probably tell

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.224
if I were in that position

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.493
of the Ukrainian military

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.262
to just press on with what

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:09.929
they're already

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.264
they've already gone under way

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:14.500
and let the disarray take,

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.968
you know, take its course

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.670
among the Russians.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.172
The thing you want to

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:19.806
think about

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:22.542
is if you get very aggressive right now,

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:26.379
will that provoke a a counter

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.548
retaliatory retaliation

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:30.616
that we might not want to see?

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.919
So I think they just need to know

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:33.753
what they're doing.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:36.689
And I think the demoralization

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.491
and the incompetence of the Russian

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.826
military is probably going

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:42.028
to be emphasized

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.896
even more because of this.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.031
This event,

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.933
more questions about their will to fight.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.034
Director James Clapper,

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.569
thanks so much for joining us, Jim.

